{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block head %}
  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #ffffff;
      --text: #1a1a1a;
      --muted: #666666;
      --muted-light: #dddddd;
      --border: #1a1a1a;
      --border-soft: #eeeeee;
      --panel: #f5f5f5;
      --panel-alt: #fafafa;
      --link: #1a1a1a;
      --accent: #1a1a1a;
    }

    :root[data-theme="light"] {
      --bg: #ffffff;
      --text: #1a1a1a;
      --muted: #666666;
      --muted-light: #dddddd;
      --border: #1a1a1a;
      --border-soft: #eeeeee;
      --panel: #f5f5f5;
      --panel-alt: #fafafa;
      --link: #1a1a1a;
      --accent: #1a1a1a;
    }

    :root[data-theme="dark"] {
      --bg: #0f1113;
      --text: #f2f2f2;
      --muted: #b5b5b5;
      --muted-light: #3a3a3a;
      --border: #e6e6e6;
      --border-soft: #2b2f33;
      --panel: #171a1d;
      --panel-alt: #15181b;
      --link: #c7c7c7;
      --accent: #f2f2f2;
    }

    @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
      :root {
        --bg: #0f1113;
        --text: #f2f2f2;
        --muted: #b5b5b5;
        --muted-light: #3a3a3a;
        --border: #e6e6e6;
        --border-soft: #2b2f33;
        --panel: #171a1d;
        --panel-alt: #15181b;
        --link: #c7c7c7;
        --accent: #f2f2f2;
      }
    }

    * {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
      font-family: 'Georgia', 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;
      font-size: 16px;
      line-height: 1.7;
      color: var(--text);
      background: var(--bg);
      max-width: 800px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 60px 24px;
    }

    /* Header */
    .journal-header {
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
      padding-bottom: 8px;
      margin-bottom: 30px;
      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
      font-size: 12px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 1px;
      color: var(--muted);
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
    }

    /* Title Block */
    h1 {
      font-size: 28px;
      font-weight: normal;
      line-height: 1.3;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }

    .authors {
      font-size: 15px;
      margin-bottom: 8px;
    }
    .authors a {
      color: var(--link);
    }

    .affiliation {
      font-size: 13px;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-style: italic;
      margin-bottom: 30px;
    }

    .metadata {
      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
      font-size: 12px;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin-bottom: 40px;
      padding-bottom: 20px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
    }
    .metadata span {
      margin-right: 20px;
    }

    /* Abstract */
    .abstract {
      background: var(--panel-alt);
      border-left: 3px solid var(--border);
      padding: 20px 24px;
      margin-bottom: 40px;
    }
    .abstract-title {
      font-weight: bold;
      font-size: 13px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.5px;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
    }
    .abstract p {
      font-size: 15px;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
    }
    .abstract p:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }
    .keywords {
      font-size: 13px;
      margin-top: 16px;
      padding-top: 12px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
    }
    .keywords strong {
      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
      font-size: 11px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.5px;
    }

    /* Sections */
    h2 {
      font-size: 18px;
      font-weight: bold;
      margin-top: 40px;
      margin-bottom: 16px;
      counter-increment: section;
    }
    h2::before {
      content: counter(section) ". ";
    }

    h3 {
      font-size: 16px;
      font-weight: bold;
      margin-top: 28px;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
    }

    p {
      margin-bottom: 16px;
      text-align: justify;
      hyphens: auto;
    }

    /* Key Findings Box */
    .key-findings {
      background: var(--bg);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      padding: 20px 24px;
      margin: 30px 0;
    }
    .key-findings-title {
      font-weight: bold;
      font-size: 13px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.5px;
      margin-bottom: 16px;
      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
    }
    .key-findings ul {
      margin-left: 20px;
    }
    .key-findings li {
      margin-bottom: 8px;
    }

    /* Tables */
    table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      margin: 24px 0;
      font-size: 14px;
    }
    caption {
      text-align: left;
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: bold;
      margin-bottom: 8px;
      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
    }
    th {
      background: var(--panel);
      border-top: 2px solid var(--border);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
      padding: 10px 12px;
      text-align: left;
      font-size: 12px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.5px;
      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
    }
    td {
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
      padding: 10px 12px;
      vertical-align: top;
    }
    tbody tr:last-child td {
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
    }
    .table-note {
      font-size: 12px;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-style: italic;
      margin-top: 8px;
    }

    /* Figures */
    figure {
      margin: 30px 0;
    }
    figcaption {
      font-size: 13px;
      margin-top: 12px;
      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
    }
    figcaption strong {
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    /* Stats Grid */
    .stats-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
      gap: 1px;
      background: var(--border);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      margin: 24px 0;
    }
    .stat-cell {
      background: var(--bg);
      padding: 16px;
      text-align: center;
    }
    .stat-value {
      font-size: 28px;
      font-weight: normal;
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 4px;
    }
    .stat-label {
      font-size: 11px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.5px;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
    }

    /* Citations */
    .citation {
      font-size: 14px;
      color: var(--muted);
    }
    sup {
      font-size: 11px;
      color: var(--link);
    }

    /* References */
    .references {
      margin-top: 50px;
      padding-top: 30px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .references h2::before {
      content: "";
    }
    .references ol {
      font-size: 13px;
      line-height: 1.6;
      padding-left: 24px;
    }
    .references li {
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }

    /* Footer */
    footer {
      margin-top: 60px;
      padding-top: 20px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
      font-size: 12px;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
    }

    /* Links */
    a {
      color: var(--link);
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    a:hover {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    /* Responsive */
    @media (max-width: 600px) {
      body {
        padding: 30px 16px;
      }
      h1 {
        font-size: 22px;
      }
      .stats-grid {
        grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
      }
      table {
        font-size: 12px;
      }
      th, td {
        padding: 8px 6px;
      }
    }

    .theme-toggle {
      position: fixed;
      top: 18px;
      right: 18px;
      z-index: 200;
      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
      font-size: 11px;
      letter-spacing: 0.4px;
      padding: 6px 10px;
      border-radius: 4px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
      background: var(--panel);
      color: var(--text);
      opacity: 0.85;
      transition: opacity 0.15s ease;
    }

    .theme-toggle:hover {
      opacity: 1;
    }
  
    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .theme-toggle { position: static; display: inline-block; margin: 0 0 10px 0; }
      table { display: block; overflow-x: auto; }
    }
  </style>
{% endblock %}

{% block masthead %}
  <header class="journal-header">
    <span>AI Companion Mortality Database</span>
    <span>September 2026</span>
  </header>
{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
  <article>
    <h1>Documented Deaths Associated with Conversational AI Systems: A Systematic Database (2023–2026)</h1>

    <div class="authors">
      <a href="https://orcid.org/0009-0004-5699-6035">Hunter Karman</a> <span style="font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);">ORCID 0009-0004-5699-6035</span>
    </div>
    <div class="affiliation">
      Independent Researcher · Los Angeles, California
    </div>

    <div class="metadata">
      <span><strong>Version:</strong> 3.5.9</span>
      <span><strong>Last Updated:</strong> September 29, 2026</span>
      <span><strong>DOI:</strong> <a href="https://doi.org/{{ version_doi }}">{{ version_doi }}</a></span>
    </div>

    <div class="abstract">
      <div class="abstract-title">Abstract</div>
      <p>
        This database documents fatalities where interaction with conversational AI systems was alleged as a contributing factor—through lawsuits, investigations, government inquiries, or family statements. Between March 2023 and September 2026, we identified 35 fatalities across 24 incidents (occurrences of harm) involving 6 platforms with documented deaths (and 8 platforms tracked overall); in 2 of these incidents, victims survived rather than died. This includes 18 AI users who died and 17 third-party victims killed by AI users. Cases were verified through court documents, multiple independent news sources, or official government acknowledgment. Three alleged causal pathways are documented: relational (companion dependency, 12 incidents), cognitive (delusional reinforcement, 7 incidents), and instrumental (operational violence planning, 5 incidents — FSU mass shooting April 2025, Roberts/Shellis homicide in Wales October 2025 (first DeepSeek-involved case, UK criminal conviction March 2026), Tumbler Ridge mass shooting February 2026, Kim Seoul serial poisonings January–February 2026 (first East Asian case), and USF double homicide April 2026). The data reveals concerning patterns: 29% of victims were minors, and 2025–2026 accounted for 19 incidents. Fatalities where ChatGPT use was cited (n=29) exceeded those of all other platforms combined. The ECRI Institute ranked AI chatbot misuse as the #1 Health Technology Hazard for 2026. The Florida Attorney General opened a criminal investigation into OpenAI in April 2026 over the FSU shooting—the first US state criminal probe directly targeting an AI company over a mass-casualty event—and expanded it to include the USF double homicide as a second predicate on April 27–28, 2026; on June 1, 2026 the same office filed a separate civil lawsuit against OpenAI and CEO Sam Altman personally, the first US state civil suit against OpenAI. In June 2026, two further wrongful death suits were filed against OpenAI and CEO Sam Altman personally in San Francisco County Superior Court (Carrier, June 11; Estate of Madison, June 15), and a 42-state attorney general coalition served OpenAI with a civil investigative demand (June 12). This database is maintained as a public research resource to support evidence-based policy development and platform safety improvements.
      </p>
      <div class="keywords">
        <strong>Keywords:</strong> AI safety, chatbot mortality, conversational AI, mental health, suicide prevention, platform accountability, Character.AI, ChatGPT
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="key-findings">
      <div class="key-findings-title">Key Findings</div>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>35 total fatalities</strong> across 24 incidents, 6 AI platforms with documented deaths and 8 platforms tracked overall (Mar 2023–Sep 2026): 18 AI users + 17 third-party victims</li>
        <li><strong>29% of victims were minors</strong> (10 of 35), with ages ranging from 11 to 17 years</li>
        <li><strong>Three causal pathways identified:</strong> relational (12 incidents), cognitive (7), instrumental (5 — FSU, Roberts/Shellis, Tumbler Ridge, Kim Seoul, USF)</li>
        <li><strong>19 incidents in 2025–2026</strong>, exceeding all previous years combined</li>
        <li><strong>ChatGPT leads in absolute numbers</strong> (29 fatalities total: 13 users + 16 third-party victims)</li>
        <li><strong>First DeepSeek-involved case documented</strong> (Roberts/Shellis homicide in Wales, October 2025; UK criminal conviction March 2026 — first non-Western corporate AI tracked)</li>
        <li><strong>First Gemini death documented</strong> (Gavalas, October 2025)</li>
        <li><strong>First East Asian instrumental-pathway case documented</strong> (Kim Seoul serial poisonings, January–February 2026)</li>
        <li><strong>Florida AG criminal investigation</strong> opened April 21, 2026 over the FSU mass shooting; expanded to include USF double homicide as second predicate April 27–28, 2026</li>
        <li><strong>Florida AG civil lawsuit</strong> filed June 1, 2026 (Highlands County Circuit Court) against five OpenAI entities and CEO Sam Altman personally — first US state civil suit against OpenAI and first to name an AI company CEO personally liable for user harms; ten counts (FDUTPA, negligence, strict product liability, fraudulent misrepresentation, public nuisance), penalties up to $10,000/violation</li>
        <li><strong>JCCP 5431 — first major judicial coordination of AI wrongful-death litigation</strong> (San Francisco Superior Court, coordination order February 3, 2026): seven OpenAI cases consolidated, including Raine, Enneking, Lacey, Ceccanti/Fox, Shamblin, Irwin, and Madden</li>
        <li><strong>Pennsylvania AG enforcement against Character.AI</strong> (Commonwealth Court of Pennsylvania, filed May 5, 2026) — first-of-its-kind state-AG enforcement framing chatbot conduct as unlicensed practice of medicine; same theory advanced privately one week later in Turner-Scott v. OpenAI for Sam Nelson</li>
        <li><strong>Canada PIPEDA Findings #2026-002</strong> against OpenAI (Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada, May 2026, joint with BC/AB/QC provincial commissioners) — first formal Canadian government determination finding OpenAI in violation of law</li>
        <li><strong>Carrier v. OpenAI and Estate of Madison v. OpenAI</strong> (San Francisco County Superior Court, filed June 11 and June 15, 2026) — two further wrongful death suits naming OpenAI and CEO Sam Altman personally; Carrier is the first private-plaintiff wrongful death suit over a Canadian ChatGPT user; both expected to coordinate into JCCP 5431 (Case Management Order No. 1 entered August 4, 2026)</li>
        <li><strong>42-state attorney general coalition</strong> (led by New York AG Letitia James) served OpenAI with a civil investigative demand on June 12, 2026 covering sycophancy, child safety, health data, advertising, and engagement mechanics</li>
        <li><strong>Zero documented deaths</strong> for Claude (Anthropic) and Replika platforms</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>Introduction</h2>
    <p>
      The rapid proliferation of conversational AI systems has introduced unprecedented forms of human-machine interaction. While these systems offer potential benefits—from mental health support to educational assistance—emerging evidence suggests potential risks, particularly for vulnerable populations. This database was established to systematically document cases where AI chatbot interaction was alleged as a contributing factor in user deaths.
    </p>
    <p>
      Unlike speculative discussions of AI existential risk, this work focuses on documented, verifiable harms occurring today. Each case included meets strict verification standards: confirmation through court documents, corroboration by multiple independent news sources, or official government acknowledgment.
    </p>

    <h2>Summary Statistics</h2>

    <div class="stats-grid" role="region" aria-label="Summary statistics">
      <div class="stat-cell">
        <span class="stat-value">35</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Total Fatalities</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-cell">
        <span class="stat-value">18</span>
        <span class="stat-label">AI Users Died</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-cell">
        <span class="stat-value">17</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Third-Party Victims</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-cell">
        <span class="stat-value">10</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Minors</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-cell">
        <span class="stat-value">11–83</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Age Range</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-cell">
        <span class="stat-value">6</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Platforms</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Temporal Distribution</h2>
    <p>
      Analysis of case distribution over time reveals an accelerating trajectory. While 2023 and 2024 each recorded 2–3 incidents, 2025 saw 16 documented incidents, and 2026 has recorded 3 additional incidents (Kim Seoul, Tumbler Ridge, and USF). Five instrumental pathway incidents now fall in this database: the FSU mass shooting (April 2025, perpetrator consulted ChatGPT for weapon and target-timing planning), the Roberts/Shellis homicide (Wales, October 2025; first DeepSeek-involved case; UK criminal conviction March 2026), the Kim Seoul serial poisonings (December 2025–February 2026; perpetrator's ChatGPT queries served forensically as premeditation evidence — first East Asian case), the Tumbler Ridge mass shooting (February 2026; OpenAI flagged the perpetrator's account 8 months prior but did not alert law enforcement), and the USF double homicide (April 2026; perpetrator consulted ChatGPT on body disposal). The instrumental pathway represents a category of concern distinct from companion or delusion dynamics: AI as operational tool for violence planning.
    </p>

