    <h2>Demographic Patterns</h2>
    <p>
      Victims ranged in age from 11 to 83 years, with a mean age of 30.5 years (Seoul victims estimated at ~25 each per midpoint of "in their 20s" source reporting). Minors (under 18) represented 29% of fatalities (10 of 35), a disproportionate figure given that minors constitute a smaller percentage of AI chatbot users. This includes 6 third-party victims (stepbrother age 11 and 5 students aged 12–13 in the Tumbler Ridge mass shooting). The two fatalities added in v3.5.0 (Christian Faith Madison, 29; Alice Carrier, 24) fall in the 18–35 age group, as did the four added in v3.4.0 (USF victims Zamil Limon 27, Nahida Bristy 27; Seoul victims ~25, ~25).
    </p>

